# {{ distribution_name }}

A standalone **scenario package** for the
[`autoware-carla-scenario`](https://github.com/hakuturu583/autoware_carla_scenario)
framework, generated with `scenario-new`. Its scenario and config dataclass
live here, outside the framework.

## Layout

```
{{ package_name }}/
├── pyproject.toml                     # declares the entry point
└── src/{{ package_name }}/
    ├── __init__.py                    # register() — the entry point target
    ├── {{ scenario_name }}.py         # the scenario class (BaseScenario)
    ├── configs.py                     # the scenario's config dataclass
    └── conf/scenario/{{ scenario_name }}/
        └── default.yaml               # a concrete scenario (YAML)
```

`tests/test_typecheck.py` (next to `src/`) runs the static check on the scenario.

## Use it

```bash
# Install into the same environment as the framework.
uv pip install -e .

# Run the scenario — it is discoverable by name, no framework edits required.
uv run scenario scenario={{ scenario_name }}/default map=nishishinjuku

# Batch/glob and CLI overrides work exactly like the built-ins:
uv run scenario scenario='{{ scenario_name }}/*' map=nishishinjuku
uv run scenario scenario={{ scenario_name }}/default scenario.timeout_seconds=20
```

## Check it

The static check compiles each scenario with Codon and reports a type error,
a misspelled config key or a bad value at its line, before CARLA starts (see
the framework's *Static Check* documentation):

```bash
# Only this package's scenarios: about 15 s per config.
uv run scenario-check scenario='{{ scenario_name }}/*'

# One config, with the same overrides as the runner takes.
uv run scenario-check scenario={{ scenario_name }}/default scenario.timeout_seconds=20
```

`scenario-check` without arguments (or `scenario='*'`) checks every installed
scenario, the built-in ones too, which takes minutes. The exit status is 0 when
every config passed, 1 when one failed the check, and 2 when it could not run:
no Codon compiler, no config matching `scenario=`, or an override of a key
the config does not have (the message suggests the closest key).

`tests/test_typecheck.py` runs the same check under pytest (`uv run pytest`).

## Ship it as a container

`pack-scenario-image` builds an image holding this package, the framework and
its CARLA client (typesafe_carla, at the version the framework's lock pins):

```yaml
- uses: hakuturu583/autoware_carla_scenario/.github/actions/pack-scenario-image@master
  with:
    scenario-package-path: {{ package_name }}
    image: ghcr.io/<owner>/{{ distribution_name }}
```

Pin a release tag instead of `main` for a reproducible framework version. See
the framework's *Container Image* documentation for the inputs and for building
the same image by hand.

## How it plugs in

`register()` in `__init__.py` calls `register_scenario(...)` and
`register_conf_dir(...)`; the `autoware_carla_scenario.scenarios` entry point in
`pyproject.toml` makes the `scenario` CLI discover it automatically at start-up.
